ner, which is strategically dangerous as it often gives the corner to the opponent.\n- Move (H, 7) is a C-square move adjacent to an empty corner, also risky, though the opponent might not be able to take the corner immediately.\n- Move (H, 8) allows me to occupy the bottom-right corner.\n- Move (H, 6) is an edge move but less valuable than the corner.\n\nReason: Taking a corner is a fundamental strategy in Reversi/Othello because corner pieces can never be flipped by the opponent. Securing H8 stabilizes that section of the board, anchors my position, and prevents the opponent from taking it later. It is far superior to playing adjacent to the corner (like G8 or H7).\n\nAnswer: (H, 8)'}
